(In UiPath Orchestrator, robots process queue items based on a strict hierarchical set of rules. The) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 305.7785436893203723 Td
(primary sorting criterion is always Priority \(High, then Normal, then Low\). Within the exact same) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 287.7785436893203723 Td
(priority level, items configured with a Deadline are processed before items without a deadline. For) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 269.7785436893203723 Td
(items sharing both the same priority and having deadlines, the one with the earliest deadline is) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 251.7785436893203723 Td
(processed first. Finally, if items are tied on priority and deadline \(or lack thereof\), they are) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 233.7785436893203723 Td
(processed based on their enqueue time in a First-In-First-Out \(FIFO\) manner. Applying this: High) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 215.7785436893203723 Td
(items \(2, 3, 6\) go first, Normal items \(4, 8, 1\) second, and Low items \(7, 5, 9\) last, each sorted) Tj
ET
