(In UiPath, string manipulations use VB.NET expressions. The Substring\(startIndex, length\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 521.8899999999999864 Td
(method extracts a substring from a string instance. The startIndex is a zero-based index, meaning) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 503.8899999999999864 Td
(the first character is at index 0, the second at index 1, and so on. To get four characters starting) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 485.8899999999999864 Td
(with the second character \(index 1\), the correct expression is StrVar.Substring\(1, 4\). This starts at) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 467.8899999999999864 Td
(the second character and extracts a total of four characters.) Tj
ET
