/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 557.8899999999999864 Td
(The "Get Mail" activities in UiPath \(such as Get Outlook, IMAP, or POP3 Mail Messages\) are) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 539.8899999999999864 Td
(designed to retrieve multiple emails from a server or client. The output of these activities is a) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 521.8899999999999864 Td
(collection of email objects. The correct variable type to hold this collection is) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 503.8899999999999864 Td
(System.Collections.Generic.List, which allows the automation to iterate through each email and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 485.8899999999999864 Td
(access its properties like Subject, Body, and Sender.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12.5 Tf
14.3749999999999982 TL
0. g
40. 453.8899999999999864 Td
(Why Incorrect Options are Wrong:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 431.8899999999999864 Td
(A. A String can only hold text, not a complex email object with its various properties and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 413.8899999999999864 Td
(attachments.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 395.8899999999999864 Td
(B. List could hold a list of subjects or senders, but not the complete email objects themselves.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 377.8899999999999864 Td
(C. MailMessage represents a single email message, whereas the activity retrieves a collection of) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 359.8899999999999864 Td
(messages, not just one.) Tj
