(In UiPath \(which utilizes VB.NET syntax\), DataTable rows and columns are zero-indexed. The) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 751.8899999999999864 Td
(expression DT.Rows\(0\)\(1\).ToString + DT.Rows\(1\)\(0\).ToString is evaluated in two parts. First,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 733.8899999999999864 Td
(DT.Rows\(0\)\(1\) accesses the first row \(index 0, corresponding to Michael\) and the second column) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 715.8899999999999864 Td
(\(index 1, corresponding to Age\), fetching the value 42. The .ToString method converts this integer) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 697.8899999999999864 Td
(to the string "42". Second, DT.Rows\(1\)\(0\) accesses the second row \(index 1, corresponding to) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 679.8899999999999864 Td
(Clara\) and the first column \(index 0, corresponding to Name\), fetching the string "Clara". Finally,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0. g
60. 661.8899999999999864 Td
(the + operator concatenates these two strings, yielding the final result of "42Clara".) Tj
ET
